WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.440
It's here ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.120
the new series from the minds behind True Detective and The Leftovers.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.180
It promises to be a mind-bending ride,

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.960
so I hope you'll join me in discovering

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.560
the secrets held within.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.560
So take your pills and put your helmets on,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.540
it's gonna be one hell of a trip.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.420
The episode begins with a crash course

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.840
in how the universe came to be,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.860
billions of years of history condensed in under a minute.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.280
But the voice-over here,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.380
likely read by Justin Theroux's character

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.420
who doesn't appear in this episode,

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.740
pays close attention to one particular moment,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:36.320
how an amoeba mutated and became the ancestor of everything we come to know on this planet.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.400
He explains that one little event

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.940
can have an impact so huge,

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.460
as to change the course of history.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.060
What he's preparing us for are the clinical trials to come.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.500
Imagine if one drug could solve our sorrows,

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.480
our deepest insecurities.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.620
Imagine how that would affect the course of history.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.320
You might also notice he uses the word "corollary" a few times,

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.540
almost as if what he's saying to us is from an academic paper he's writing.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.960
Annie Landsberg, played here by Emma Stone,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.280
wants to buy some cigarettes, but the clerk doesn't accept "Ad Buddy".

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.860
"Ad Buddy" is an organization that controls almost every aspect of advertisement.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.680
It's as pervasive if not more than Google or Apple is today.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.740
We'll get to know a little bit more about "Ad Buddy" later on.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.980
The clerk says "Ad Buddy" isn't accepted because

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.380
the national database of desires uses it

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.700
to collect data and control people.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.620
A slight jab at companies like Facebook

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.060
who've been known to sell data to say ...

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.340
Influence elections.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.000
Annie jimmies a lock to get some change when we see the newspaper headline,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.040
"Bladdergate, Milgram poop bot empire in peril".

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.000
This is a nod to Owen Milgram's family who we'll meet in a bit.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.450
She passes men in suits exchanging briefcases.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.300
These are men who work for "Ad Buddy",

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.740
making their money by personally delivering ads to the consumer.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.200
In a cafe, Annie watches a man recollect a story on

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.340
how he somehow got to Poland and wasn't sure how.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.840
But it probably has something to do with the pin he wears on his chest,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.720
a symbol that shows up in the next scene.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.280
The voice-over continues to pontificate on how we're all connected.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.780
All souls are on a quest to connect,

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.540
and without that connection we feel lost.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:14.140
This hints at what the show is really about, playing on themes of loneliness and man's purpose in the world.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.000
A lot of our characters we'll find have lost that connection and thus feel empty,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.680
searching for pills to make them feel better.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.240
We see an ad for "doxed",

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.920
a service that helps when your online identity is stolen

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.140
or revealed to others, before it switches to this one, stating

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.880
"everything tastes better when you're together".

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.360
And look at that, it's the same symbol found on the cafe guy's shirt.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.420
On the other side of the post is an ad,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.500
"not all hugs are created equal"

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.120
by Dr. Greta Mantelray.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.160
She'll show up again later too.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.800
Annie passes a poop bot display in front of Milgram Industries.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.520
A whole ton of garbage is trashed on the sidewalk like it's out of business.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.640
Notice here the book of Don Quixote the story of a man who loses his sanity and decides to become a knight.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.740
A man who does not see the world for what it is, but what he dreams it to be.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.640
The voice-over ends with the man stating his main goal,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.760
"... to eliminate all unnecessary and inefficient forms of human pain",

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.700
something tells me he's connected to Neberdine Pharmaceuticals later on.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.720
The maniac logo appears on screen looking eerily similar to that of IBM's in the 1980s,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.780
a computer company large, cold

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.780
and devoid of the emotion and humanity our voice-over guy claimed humanity was all about.

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:31.220
We then meet Owen Milgram, his last name a nod to the Milgram experiments of the 1960s

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:34.960
which gauged a participants willingness to obey an authority figure,

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.780
even if it conflicted with their personal conscious.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:43.260
This usually involved the subject being told to administer increasing amounts of electrical shocks to an actor,

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.560
even if it caused them extreme pain.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.860
What they found, most of the subjects obeyed the authority.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:53.100
Back to Owen, he's being tested for an upcoming trials against his brother Jed.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:58.240
His dad is there helping him and we learn he's experienced a psychotic breakdown ten years ago.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.040
He recounts his story of how he was hospitalized while playing with a Rubik's Cube,

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.840
just like the one found outside his offices.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.300
It appears he sees his brother Jed when he's not really there,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.220
he lies when asked if he knows what's really real,

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:17.600
stating his "compos mentis", Latin for stable mind, not mentioning his vision of the water rumbling on his desk.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.620
The Statue of Liberty has been replaced with The Statue of Extra Liberty,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.180
a winged God threatening, holding a lightning bolt and head,

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:29.920
whereas the Statue of Liberty was a beacon, a light to welcome immigrants from around the world.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.340
The Statue of Extra Liberty is a warning

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.400
"Stay out or feel its wrath".

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:39.220
At tour passes with people wearing what seems like manga hats, minus the logo.

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:43.580
And the tour guide is Russian, all seeming to be a veiled jab at President Donald Trump

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.300
and the Russian collusion scandal.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.700
Notice how their hats are embroidered with the number "47",

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.600
suggesting the 47th President of the United States,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.609
meaning in this world, we are anywhere from 6 to 14 years in the future.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.522
Also important to note are their fishermen wearing logos of companies,

00:04:59.522 --> 00:05:02.700
almost as if they've leased their bodies to corporations,

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:08.580
a juxtaposition between the supposed freedom of the Statue but being slaves to corporations,

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.780
the ones who make the real decisions.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.120
Owen's imaginary brother Jed arrives, who tells him he's been chosen to save the world,

00:05:15.126 --> 00:05:18.180
a woman will reach out to him with further instructions.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.880
But this is seemingly all a dream as the popcorn he was feeding the birds begins to pop.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.700
Owen tries to buy a transit pass but he's out of money,

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.020
looks like in the future technology has really gone downhill.

00:05:29.029 --> 00:05:33.301
There's an interesting ad to travel to the moon next to an "Ad Buddies Wanted" sign.

00:05:33.301 --> 00:05:36.940
Speaking of "Ad Buddy", Owen is accompanied on his commute home by one,

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.240
they pass a fun sign of the repercussions of attacking a poop bot,

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:43.740
while on the train he's bombarded with ads delivered personally by him.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.940
"Ad Buddy" asked if he's considered doing clinical trials for a pharmaceutical company called "Neberdine",

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.280
while Owen envisions Annie in an ad for "Daddy's Home",

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.820
a company that brings single guys in, as voluntary husbands, for women who've lost their spouses,

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.560
in return for companionship.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.660
To make matters worse for Owen, he finds out he's on furlough,

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.640
permanently.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.940
He throws up in the toilet where even the paper has ads on it.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:12.160
Frustrated, he rips off the dispenser to find the same words his imaginary brother said to him,

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.817
"the pattern is the pattern".

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:20.140
Owen listens to a tape in what seems to be some form of therapist who knows all about his mental frustrations,

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:23.200
how he needs a partner to finish a mission his brother sent him on

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.620
while we see Annie in yet another ad.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:29.800
Whether that is actually her or part of his imagination is yet to be seen.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.121
At home, we see he's on several medications and has a self-help book

00:06:33.121 --> 00:06:35.900
by the same author we saw Annie pass in the ad.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.080
The man on the tape says everything Jed says is a lie,

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.539
trying to ground Owen back in reality.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.680
He flicks his pills,

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:46.880
and judging by the amount of them in his plant, hasn't been taking them for some time.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:52.980
He receives a package from Neberdine Pharmaceuticals and a call stating that he qualifies as a hero candidate.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:56.680
Notice also the two diametrically opposed ads in the background,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.720
one for toothpaste and the other for Jolly Ranchers.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.580
He's a candidate to treat those suffering from depression and other popcorn problems.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.475
Is he really hearing this or is it all in his mind?

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:12.360
At this point, it should be noted that we can't take everything from Owens perspective at face value,

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.400
he's not a reliable narrator.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.460
Owen goes to his mom and dad's for dinner,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.660
catching the final moments of his brother's barbershop medley.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:23.920
Notice Jed here not imaginary, doesn't dawn a mustache.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.540
The founding father of the family has a picture of what looks like George Washington behind him,

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.840
the first president and founding father of the United States.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.060
There's a giant painting of the family and Owen's not in it.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.680
Jed's fiancé hasn't agreed to marry him until Owen is painted in.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.214
She's on meds of her own and

00:07:40.214 --> 00:07:42.240
Owen talks about going away with her,

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.016
starting a new life with new identities,

00:07:45.016 --> 00:07:45.780
as friends.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.620
We're given a bit more info on Jed,

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.293
apparently Owen was a witness to whatever scandal he was involved in

00:07:51.293 --> 00:07:52.860
and reassures his family that

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.200
Jed didn't do it.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.120
Notice here, the rainbow and the painting.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.260
One, it's very odd,

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:00.200
and two, it fits in in one of the Neberdine's slogans,

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.600
"follow the rainbow".

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.024
Owen lashes out at his family

00:08:03.024 --> 00:08:04.940
and his father walks him to the subway.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:07.108
He wants to help his son, buy him a home,

00:08:07.108 --> 00:08:09.100
work for the company like his brothers,

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.440
but he doesn't want to.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.500
Owen tells him he doesn't have to buy him off,

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.160
he'll be the good son and lie for Jed.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.600
Apparently Jed is involved in some scandal involving a woman,

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.920
who his father says is

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.120
"just trying to take advantage of the family".

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.374
Owen lies to his father,

00:08:23.374 --> 00:08:24.743
telling him he's got a new job

00:08:24.743 --> 00:08:26.340
and that he'll be away for a while.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.560
But he's really off to Neberdine to be a part of the trials.

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:34.760
We also get a quick shot of one of the poop bot in action, leaving a blue sanitary liquid behind.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.860
Again more, rainbow symbolism.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.380
At Neberdine Pharmaceuticals,

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.300
he fills out a form when another patient asked him what trial he's there for.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:47.280
He says ULP which apparently is the big time where you'll make a lot of money.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.180
The bombs on the forum mean high risk,

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.767
hence why you get paid a lot.

00:08:50.767 --> 00:08:53.120
He watches as Annie storms out of the room,

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.780
apparently pissed off about some thing,

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.760
before he's called into the screening room.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.920
There, he's asked to describe in a word the pictures he sees,

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.080
pills, a hawk and family,

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.340
All things he's dealt with recently.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:07.440
The picture of the family, he associates with suffocation.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.520
It's quite obvious what he thinks about them.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:13.440
The screener then says she's going to ask Owen one final question,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:18.200
but she just stares at him before the green light turns on and we learn he's been accepted.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:23.124
His defence mechanisms are fungible, meaning interchangeable with another.

00:09:23.124 --> 00:09:26.839
The screener bows, suggesting there is some sort of Japanese connection,

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.280
like if you remember the Japanese businessmen out front,

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:33.420
perhaps they are the ones fronting the money for these trials.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.960
Owen confronts Annie asking her if she'd lost her husband recently or plays golf at Hilton Head,

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.020
referring to the ads he's been seeing her in.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.300
She's called away when Owens haunted by Jed,

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:48.300
he says Annie is her handler and that he needs to make contact with her by using the code phrase,

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.815
"the pattern is the pattern".

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:54.500
They are taken deep into Neberdine's lab, where we meet Dr. Fujita and Morimoto.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:58.940
The odd numbered patients have arrived and they must continue without any of the old problems.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:03.454
He's wearing a weird headphone contraption around his ears and seems to be sleep-deprived,

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:06.160
or just overdosed from the crack he keeps in his drawer.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.300
The subjects are escorted to the pod room where they'll be staying for the duration of the trial.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.940
The orderly goes over the rules,

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:14.120
no intimacy, cohabitation,

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:19.060
and any unauthorized absence for the pod will result in the termination of the trial.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.087
Owen goes to Annie and gives her the code,

00:10:21.087 --> 00:10:24.080
but she doesn't seem to know what the hell he's talking about.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.580
But as he begins to break down,

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.720
Annie fearing she might get kicked out due to his outburst,

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:29.820
goes along with it,

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.460
telling him to wait further instructions so they can save the world together.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:38.007
They are then greeted by Dr. Morimoto and Fujita, who will be supervising them.

00:10:38.007 --> 00:10:42.000
Fujita takes out a cigarette and Morimoto tells them not to fuck this up.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.680
Clearly these two aren't the most professional.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.580
What will happen as this trial begins?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.600
And where's the even-numbered test group?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.500
Will Owen receive further instructions from Annie and save the world?

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.000
We'll have to tune in to episode 2 to find out.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.700
Thanks everyone for watching,

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.080
this show is really trippy

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.340
and I think warranted an explain series,

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.880
so I hope you'll like, subscribe and follow me on this journey.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.500
Stay tuned for episode 2.

